{% if slide_title %}
HEADER (draw exactly as written, in this order; skip a line that is absent):
{% if label %}
  kicker: {{ label }}
{% endif %}
  headline: {{ slide_title }}
{% if subtitle %}
  subtitle: {{ subtitle }}
{% endif %}
{% if core_hook %}
DECK NARRATIVE: {{ core_hook }}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
OBJECTIVE: {{ objective }}
{% endif %}
{% if slide_type %}
SLIDE TYPE: {{ slide_type }}
{% endif %}

COMPONENTS (put every one on the slide — each carries its own data):
{% for comp in components %}
- {{ comp.kind }}{% if comp.component_id %} [{{ comp.component_id }}]{% endif %}{% if comp.count > 1 %} (x{{ comp.count }}){% endif %}{% if comp.chart_type %} [{{ comp.chart_type }}]{% endif %}{% if comp.content_summary %}: {{ comp.content_summary }}{% endif +%}
{% if comp.weight and comp.weight != "peer" %}  height-weight: {{ comp.weight }} (see SIZING BY WEIGHT in layout grammar){% if comp.kind == "table" %}; a table's weight is rows, never grow on its card{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if comp.design_hint %}  visual-intent: {{ comp.design_hint }}
{% endif %}
{% if hint_scopes and hint_scopes.get(comp.kind) %}  scope: {{ hint_scopes[comp.kind] }}
{% endif %}
{% if comp.content_data %}
  Data for {{ comp.component_id or comp.kind }}:
  {% for key, value in comp.content_data.items() %}
  {{ key }}: {{ value }}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if layout_hint %}

LAYOUT INTENT - which regions carry weight and how the components relate
(e.g. "chart is primary, table is supporting context beside it"). This is a
priority statement, NOT pixel coordinates: turn it into bands + a %/max split
using the LAYOUT GRAMMAR. If it conflicts with the grammar's rules, the grammar wins.
{{ layout_hint }}
{% endif %}
{% if supplied_content %}

SUPPLIED CONTENT (use these values EXACTLY, verbatim):
{% for key, value in supplied_content.items() %}
{{ key }}: {{ value }}
{% endfor %}
{% elif content_data %}

SLIDE-LEVEL DATA (fallback — use per-component data above when available):
{% for key, value in content_data.items() %}
{{ key }}: {{ value }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

FIGURES: use only the figures given above, exactly as written - never make up,
round or restyle a number, a date or a source. A component with no data gets
short wording from the plan and no numbers. Never "XX%", "TBD", "Lorem ipsum",
"Company A", "Metric 1".

SIZING — follow SIZING BY WEIGHT and DATA NODE SIZING in the layout grammar.
No pixel h on bands or cards: grow (from the height-weight) on the band(s) that
should fill, h="max" minH on charts and diagrams, tables sized by their rows.
Header, KPI rows and text-only bands (callout, narrative, bullet_list) size to content.
KEEP TEXT SHORT so content-sized bands stay compact:
  Bullets: 1 line each (~50-60 chars). Callout body: 1 sentence (≤ 80 chars).
  Timeline description: 1-3 words ONLY — sentences collide in columns.
If the content is thin, give the components more room (see SIZING BY WEIGHT) -
never add content the plan does not have.

Output the POM XML for this slide - a single <Slide> element, no <Theme>, no
markdown fences, no commentary.
